+<!-- TrendForce Consumer Electronics press list, fetched 2026-10-26 01:31Z via gate-probe url-probe run 40254580918; press-item blocks copied verbatim, page chrome removed. -->
+<div class="list">
+<h3 class="font-size-18"><a class="title-link" href="/presscenter/news/20261008-13264.html"><strong>Rising Costs Threaten Notebook Demand in 2027, Raising Risks of Shipment Declines and Price Increases, Says TrendForce</strong></a></h3>
+                    <h4 class="font-size-16 color-green margin-t-10"><strong>8 October 2026</strong></h4>
+                    <p class="font-size-16">
+                        TrendForce&#039;s latest notebook industry research reveals that the primary risk facing the market in 2027 is expected to shift from supply constraints to the impact of rising costs on demand. Global notebook shipments are currently projected to decline by a low-single-digit percentage in 2027.
+                    </p>
+<h3 class="font-size-18"><a class="title-link" href="/presscenter/news/20260910-13228.html"><strong>iPhone Duo Expected to Capture Nearly 25% of Foldable Smartphone Market in 2026 as Apple’s First Foldable Drives Supply Chain Upgrades, Says TrendForce</strong></a></h3>
+                    <h4 class="font-size-16 color-green margin-t-10"><strong>10 September 2026</strong></h4>
+                    <p class="font-size-16">
+                        Apple has officially launched its first foldable smartphone, the iPhone Duo. Featuring a book-style inward-folding design, the device comes with a 7.6-inch inner display and a 5.4-inch cover display. TrendForce estimates that iPhone Duo shipments will reach approximately 5 million units in 2026, giving Apple a 24.8% share of the foldable smartphone market and making it the second-largest brand behind Samsung.
+                    </p>
+<h3 class="font-size-18"><a class="title-link" href="/presscenter/news/20260908-13222.html"><strong>Early Purchases Lift 2026 Smartphone Production Above Expectations; Full-Year Forecast Raised to 1.07 Billion Units, Says TrendForce</strong></a></h3>
+                    <h4 class="font-size-16 color-green margin-t-10"><strong>8 September 2026</strong></h4>
+                    <p class="font-size-16">
+                        Global smartphone production reached 275 million units in 2Q26, down 8% YoY, according to TrendForce’s latest smartphone industry research. The decline was narrower than previously forecast, resulting in better-than-expected overall performance.
+                    </p>
+<h3 class="font-size-18"><a class="title-link" href="/presscenter/news/20260904-13217.html"><strong>Improved CPU Supply Narrows 2026 Global Notebook Shipment Decline to 9.4%, but Brands Still Face Heavy Cost Pressure, Says TrendForce</strong></a></h3>
+                    <h4 class="font-size-16 color-green margin-t-10"><strong>4 September 2026</strong></h4>
+                    <p class="font-size-16">
+                        TrendForce’s recent research into the notebook industry shows that CPU supply has markedly improved since 2Q26, enabling brands to gradually normalize their procurement and manufacturing processes. Meanwhile, persistent increases in DRAM and SSD costs have led brands to accelerate their procurement strategies to secure components earlier, resulting in shipment volumes exceeding expectations in the first half of the year. Nonetheless, the ongoing rise in memory prices, along with increased CPU costs, has further amplified cost pressures on notebook brands.
+                    </p>
+<h3 class="font-size-18"><a class="title-link" href="/presscenter/news/20260903-13213.html"><strong>Memory Costs Drive Up iPhone 18 Series BOM; AI and Pricing to Shape Upgrade Demand, Says TrendForce</strong></a></h3>
+                    <h4 class="font-size-16 color-green margin-t-10"><strong>3 September 2026</strong></h4>
+                    <p class="font-size-16">
+                        TrendForce’s latest smartphone industry research indicates that Apple plans to adjust its product launch schedule starting in 2026, splitting new releases between fall and spring. This fall will see the debut of the flagship iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max, along with the highly anticipated iPhone 18 Fold (tentative name), Apple’s first foldable smartphone. The standard iPhone 18 and other variants are expected to follow in the first quarter of 2027.
+                    </p>
+</div>
